{{Wow-section}}
[[File:Lord Jorach Ravenholdt.jpg|thumb|upright|Jorach Ravenholdt in his [[Ravenholdt Manor|manor]].]]
Years later, Lord Jorach Ravenholdt was present in his [[Ravenholdt Manor|manor]] in the [[Alterac Mountains]] from where he led his organization and continued to fight against the [[Syndicate]]. After being stolen by some thieves, whom he had eliminated, he summoned a promising [[rogue]] [[adventurer]] to retrieve a [[Sealed Azure Bag]],<ref>[[A Simple Request]]</ref> which was sold with its secret contents as a holy relic to some [[Timbermaw Shaman]] in [[Azshara]], whether by stealing it or by the hard way, before bringing it to [[Archmage Xylem]] in [[Xylem's Tower|his tower]].<ref>[[Sealed Azure Bag (quest)]]</ref>

He asked a favor to the Archmage and the rogue adventurer to remove the enchantment that prevented the opening of the bag.<ref>[[Encoded Fragments]]</ref> Jorach Ravenholdt eventually obtained the [[Azure Key]], which the rogue adventurer brought to him after defeating a green drake known as [[Morphaz]] in the [[Temple of Atal'Hakkar]], in the [[Swamp of Sorrows]]. He thanked the rogue adventurer by allowing them to take an enchanted garment in his stores, as they are reserved for rogues of exceptional skill and loyalty.

He ended up opening the bag and was bathed in a golden glow from within, his eyes widened while he stared inside.<ref>[[The Azure Key]]</ref>

He also tasked [[Dirk Thunderwood]] to track down a new and extremely effective poison compound that could be crafted from the venom sacs of the inhabitants of [[Zul'Gurub]] and the [[Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj]].<ref>[[The Perfect Poison]]</ref>

===Cataclysm===
{{Cata-section}}
Following the [[Cataclysm (event)|Cataclysm]], Ravenholdt and his league stole [[Wrathion]]'s egg from the [[red dragonflight]],<ref>[[A Hidden Message]]</ref><ref>[[To Ravenholdt]]</ref> bringing him to Ravenholdt Manor, where he eventually hatched and began operations to exterminate the [[black dragonflight]].<ref>[[To Catch a Thief]]</ref>

At some point after her defeat in the [[Deadmines]], Lord Ravenholdt helped [[Vanessa VanCleef]] and promised her the position of the final Shadow.<ref name="Honoring Success">[[Honoring Success]]</ref>

===Legion===
{{Legion-section}}
[[File:Lord Jorach Ravenholdt Legion.jpg|thumb|left|upright|Jorach in the [[Hall of Shadows]].]]
Following the [[Battle for Broken Shore]], Jorach Ravenholdt came into contact with a rogue hero by sending a [[Ravenholdt Courier|messenger]] carrying a sealed letter, inviting them to join him alone and in complete discretion in the [[Hall of Shadows]] through his contact [["Red" Jack Findle]] in the [[Glorious Goods]] of Dalaran. In the [[Chamber of Shadows]], he met the rogue hero alongside the [[Council of Shadows]] and invited them to take their seat as the final Shadow, and help them lead the Uncrowned.<ref>[[Call of The Uncrowned]]</ref>

After the presentation of the secret organization, their methods, and their goals, Jorach Ravenholdt organized with the now complete Council of Shadows the obtaining of the legendary artifacts that are [[The Kingslayers]]: [[Anguish]] and [[Sorrow]], [[The Dreadblades]]: [[Fate]] and [[Fortune]], and the [[Fangs of the Devourer]]: [[Gorefang]] and [[Akaari's Will]], to equip their champion who would operate outside and vanquished their foes.<ref>[[A Worthy Blade]]</ref>

After successfully securing all of the artifacts, Ravenholdt was poisoned among the members of the Council of Shadows during their meeting by [[Vanessa VanCleef]], Kingpin of the [[Defias Brotherhood]], who wanted the place of the final Shadow. Following her defeat against the rogue hero, he left her no choice but to serve the latter or be executed by the Uncrowned. He then expressed his grief of imagining her [[Edwin VanCleef|father]] being disappointed in her actions.<ref name="Honoring Success" />

During the [[Burning Legion]]'s [[Third invasion of the Burning Legion|third invasion]], he began recruiting and mobilizing their agents on the Broken Isles with the help of [[Nikki the Gossip]].<ref>[[Delegation (rogue)]]</ref><ref>[[Lethal Efficiency]]</ref> Following the discovery of the body of an [[SI:7]] agent in the [[Underbelly|sewers of Dalaran]], Ravenholdt feared that the SI:7 would take too much interest in them. Subsequently, he sent his agents to investigate the situation in [[Stormwind City]],<ref>[[A Body of Evidence]]</ref> where they discovered that [[Mathias Shaw]] had increased his number of agents in Horde territory,<ref>[[Spy vs. Spy (quest)]]</ref> and ordered the elimination of [[Amber Kearnen]].<ref>[[The Bloody Truth]]</ref>

Realizing that something was wrong with Shaw's behavior, Ravenholdt sent agents of the Uncrowned to investigate the relationship between the SI:7 and the [[Red Blade]] at [[Citrine Bay]], in [[Stormheim]],<ref>[[Mystery at Citrine Bay]]</ref> where they discovered that the Spymaster ordered the pirates to execute Amber Kearnen in exchange for access to Stormwind Harbor and a royal pardon for their past crimes committed.<ref>[[Searching For Clues]]</ref> They also got their hands on a mysterious letter with a complex code that they brought to him and began to decipher it to find out the reasons for Mathias to eliminate his best agent.<ref>[[Dark Secrets and Shady Deals]]</ref>

After translating the letter and uncovering the plan of the [[dreadlord]] [[Detheroc]], leading to the rescue of [[Mathias Shaw]] and the elimination of the demon to prevent a new conflict between the Alliance and the Horde, Lord Jorach Ravenholdt rewarded the Last Shadow for their many exploits with the title of Shadowblade,<ref>[[One More Thing... (rogue)]]</ref> and also with the [[Shadowblade's Murderous Omen]] after they deal with the [[Homunculi]] alongside [[Lilian Voss]] in the Hall of Shadows and in the cities of the Alliance and the Horde.<ref>[[Dread Infiltrators]]</ref><ref>[[Hiding In Plain Sight]]</ref>

Following their victory, Lord Ravenholdt was one of the order hall champions who met [[Khadgar]] and [[Velen]] at [[Krasus' Landing]] to discuss the [[Pillars of Creation]],<ref>[[The Tomb of Sargeras trailer]]</ref> as the Uncrowned joined the other orders to form the [[Armies of Legionfall]].

===Exploring Azeroth===
{{novel-section}}
Following the [[Argus Campaign]] and the [[Fourth War]], [[Mathias Shaw|Spymaster Mathias Shaw]] mentioned in his report that the [[Uncrowned]] were still active with Jorach Ravenholdt at their head.<ref name="Exploring Azeroth" />

