==Notes and trivia==
*After being killed, players will have only 5 minutes to get the [[Stolen Treats]] and free Metzen.
**Since the [[Strange Snowman]] also provides the daily quest, if players park all their available characters, they can get between 4-5 characters done per kill.
*Prior to the 2011 version of Winter Veil, the Greench was solely responsible for the theft of the Stolen Treats; rescuing Metzen was a [[Metzen the Reindeer (quest)|separate quest]] taking place in {{Classic|Searing Gorge}} and {{Classic|Tanaris}}. The 2011 redesign combined the two by moving Metzen to the Alterac Mountains.
*The Abominable Greench is a reference to both the {{Wp|Yeti|Abominable Snowman}} and to the {{Wp|Grinch}}, the titular character of {{Wp|Dr. Seuss}}' children's book ''{{Wp|How the Grinch Stole Christmas!}}''.
*[[Grunch]] is a baby version of the Greench. The guardian pet [[Mechanical Greench]] can be contained in [[Ticking Present]], and [[Puntable Baby Greench]] can be unlocked for the [[Box of Puntables]] toy.
*A {{Hots|portrait}} depicting the Greench is available in ''[[Heroes of the Storm]]'' during Winter Veil.
*In ''[[Hearthstone (game)|Hearthstone]]'', [[Uther the Lightbringer|Uther Lightbringer]] has an alternate {{Hs|Greench Uther|Greench Uther}} skin which depicts him wearing a Greench costume.

